{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSineRiemannForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.LogSineRiemannForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSineSmoothPart"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.smooth_defect_eq_riemann_defect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.smooth_defect_eq_riemann_defect","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineRiemannForm.lean#L70-L101","doc":"**The smooth half is a right-endpoint Riemann defect (sorry-free,\nexact).**  Each cell contributes `h·φ(x_{i+1}) − ∫_{cell} φ`, so the sum\nis the Riemann sum minus the integral over `[0, nh]`.  No hypotheses\nbeyond integrability, which `φ` has everywhere. ","signatureChunk":0}]}